WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.817
Semi-structured data has some organization without requiring every record to look exactly the same.

00:00:05.817 --> 00:00:07.982
JSON is a common example.

00:00:07.982 --> 00:00:13.407
Fields have names, but values can be nested, and different records may contain different keys.

00:00:13.407 --> 00:00:19.742
That flexibility is useful for APIs, devices, logs, and fast-changing applications.

00:00:19.742 --> 00:00:23.067
The tradeoff is that analysts often need to flatten records, handle optional fields,

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:27.422
and manage schema changes before analysis.

00:00:27.422 --> 00:00:33.707
A useful project question is: what preparation step is required before analysis can even begin?

00:00:33.707 --> 00:00:38.177
A relational table may be ready for profiling, JSON may need flattening, and free text may need NLP or another

00:00:38.177 --> 00:00:41.712
extraction step.

00:00:41.712 --> 00:00:46.522
The form of the data changes the engineering path, but it does not by itself tell us whether the data is

00:00:46.522 --> 00:00:48.080
high quality.
